<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-294 - never relaunch into full screen.

  `SMainWindow::saveWindowLayout()` stored `saveGeometry()` unchanged in
  `ui/windowGeometry`, and Qt's geometry blob carries the full-screen flag.
  At the next interactive start `restoreWindowLayout()` + `show()` put the
  window back into full screen; on macOS it had never been a native
  full-screen Space, so the menu bar never came back and there was no way out.
  Every later start did the same.

  The fix has two halves and this case gates each on its own:

    RESTORE - after restoreGeometry(), a full-screen state becomes maximized
              (swindowgeometry::relaunchState). Gated by the four
              restore-window-layout lines: a full-screen blob written by Qt,
              and the 66-byte blob from the field report, restore MAXIMIZED;
              an ordinary maximized and an ordinary windowed blob restore as
              they did before.

    SAVE    - the stored blob never carries the flag
              (swindowgeometry::withoutFullScreen). Gated by the
              save-window-layout lines with windowState=: a full-screen window
              stores a blob that Qt restores maximized; maximized and windowed
              windows store what they did before.

  Every assertion is a window STATE (`windowState()`), never a rectangle: a
  "test-case" run never shows the main window, so no geometry is real, but
  the state restoreGeometry() and the fix give it is. What the platform does
  with that state at show() (on macOS: the menu bar) is hand-checked.

  THIS CASE OWNS NO SETTINGS KEY. Both verbs snapshot `ui/windowGeometry` and
  `ui/windowState`, write them back (or remove them again when they were
  absent) BEFORE they assert, and put the main window's own geometry and state
  back too.

  Watched failing on sabotaged binaries: with the relaunchState() call removed
  from restoreWindowLayout() the "fullscreen" and "report" restore lines fail
  (restored as fullscreen); with the withoutFullScreen() call removed from
  saveWindowLayout() the windowState="fullscreen" save line fails (stored
  fullscreen). The other lines pass on both, as the "as before" claim says
  they must.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="window_layout_fullscreen">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- RESTORE. A blob Qt wrote for a full-screen window relaunches
         maximized. -->
    <restore-window-layout seed="fullscreen" expectState="maximized"/>

    <!-- ...and so does the exact blob from the report: frame 0,26 to
         1279,827, maximized byte 0, full-screen byte 0x04. -->
    <restore-window-layout seed="report" expectState="maximized"/>

    <!-- As before: maximized stays maximized, windowed stays windowed. -->
    <restore-window-layout seed="maximized" expectState="maximized"/>
    <restore-window-layout seed="normal" expectState="normal"/>

    <!-- SAVE. A full-screen window stores a blob that restores maximized. -->
    <save-window-layout force="true" expectWritten="true"
                        windowState="fullscreen" expectStored="maximized"/>

    <!-- As before: maximized and windowed windows store what they are. -->
    <save-window-layout force="true" expectWritten="true"
                        windowState="maximized" expectStored="maximized"/>
    <save-window-layout force="true" expectWritten="true"
                        windowState="normal" expectStored="normal"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
